            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 18 manifest paths. The change is pure in-memory string matching over an already-loaded settings document: no I/O, retries, loops, or allocations of consequence are added, so there is no latency or load impact.",
              "engine/settings/recognize.go commandMentions now returns false for an empty word, which closes the empty-binary-path case (an earlier lens flagged it as a hardening warning). The behavior is pinned by engine/settings/query_test.go and engine/settings/recognize_test.go, and the Codex owns guard in engine/settings/codexhooks/document.go still rejects an empty binary first.",
