            "evidence": [
              "engine/settings/recognize.go: entryMentions/commandMentions preserve the prior bare-or-shell-quoted substring match over hooks[].command, and add a guard so an empty word matches nothing. This is pinned externally by engine/settings/recognize_test.go (empty binary path for CommandOwnedBy, HasHookContaining, HasLabdrianOwnedHook) and by the updated case in engine/settings/query_test.go.",
              "engine/settings/codexhooks/document.go: owns keeps the empty-binary guard first, then calls CommandOwnedBy on the handler's command string; a handler without a string command yields an empty command and is not owned. Behavior matches the former synthetic-root query.",
              "engine/status/status.go: the five hook checks now match the installed binary path plus the family token and their notes name both via referencing(). engine/status/status_test.go covers bare and quoted paths, the binary name under a different path, the binary without the family word, an empty hooks object, and every hook under another home. Goldens and the new golden case in engine/cmd/status_golden_test.go pin the user-visible note and verdict changes, which the task doc records as owner-requested.",
              "engine/settings/status.go: HasLabdrianOwnedHook delegates to hookFamily.carries, the same two-word check with the new empty-path guard; carries reads only identity, so building a bare hookFamily is safe.",
              "Residual: matching remains substring-based, so a longer path that begins with the installed path would still match for the non-projection hooks. This is pre-existing behavior and not asserted either way; no candidate-caused reliability defect found. Receipt JSON files and the task doc have no runtime effect."
            ]
